## 3. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

### Owner entity
**Path:** `/home/daniel/.../src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

Extends `Person`. Fields (with the validation constraints already on the entity):
- `address` — `@NotEmpty`
- `city` — `@NotEmpty`
- `telephone` — `@NotEmpty @Digits(fraction=0, integer=10) @Pattern(regexp="^[0-9]{10}$", message="Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")`
- `pets` — `@OneToMany` (eager)

Getters/setters: `getAddress/setAddress`, `getCity/setCity`, `getTelephone/setTelephone`, `getPets/setPets`, `addPet(Pet)`, `getPet(...)`.

**Person base class** (`/home/daniel/.../src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`) provides `firstName` and `lastName`, both `@NotEmpty`, with getters/setters. It extends `BaseEntity` (which provides `id` / `isNew()`).

### OwnerRepository
**Path:** `/home/daniel/.../src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

Available methods:
```java
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName) throws DataAccessException;   // starts-with match
Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
Owner findById(int id) throws DataAccessException;                              // throws if not found
void save(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;                              // insert or update
Collection<Owner> findAll() throws DataAccessException;
Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
void delete(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
```

Important for your question about querying by fields: **The only field-based finder is `findByLastName`.** There is NO method to query by `firstName`, `address`, `city`, or `telephone`. If you need such queries you would have to add a new method to this interface (and to its implementations — jdbc/jpa/spring-data-jpa, per the `Lookups` javadoc). The interface javadoc notes method names follow Spring Data naming conventions, so a Spring Data-style derived query method (e.g. `findByFirstNameAndLastName`) could be added.

Note `findById` does not return null on miss — it throws `ObjectRetrievalFailureException` / `EmptyResultDataAccessException`, which is translated via the shared helper `Lookups.findOrNotFound(...)` at `/home/daniel/.../src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/common/Lookups.java`.

## 4. OwnerResponse / OwnerRequest DTO classes

There are no classes literally named `OwnerResponse` or `OwnerRequest`. The DTOs are **generated from the OpenAPI contract** (they are not present in `src`; they materialize into `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` at build time). The relevant generated types are:
- `OwnerFieldsDto` — the request body for POST/PUT (editable fields)
- `OwnerDto` — the response body (extends the fields with `id` and `pets`)
- `OwnerPageDto` — a page wrapper

They are defined in the OpenAPI spec:
**Path:** `/home/daniel/.../src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (schemas start at line 1991)

```yaml
    OwnerFields:
      title: Owner fields
      description: Editable fields of a pet owner.
      type: object
      properties:
        firstName:
          title: First name
          description: The first name of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 30
          pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$"
          example: George
        lastName:
          title: Last name
          description: The last name of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 30
          pattern: "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$"
          example: Franklin
        address:
          title: Address
          description: The postal address of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 255
          example: '110 W. Liberty St.'
        city:
          title: City
          description: The city of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 80
          example: Madison
        telephone:
          title: Telephone number
          description: The telephone number of the pet owner.
          type: string
          minLength: 1
          maxLength: 20
          pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
          example: '6085551023'
      required:
        - firstName
        - lastName
        - address
        - city
        - telephone
    Owner:
      title: Owner
      description: A pet owner.
      allOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OwnerFields'
        - type: object
