The `newOwner(...)` helper (lines 49-58) shows the canonical valid owner values used across tests (firstName "George", address "110 W. Liberty St.", city "Madison", telephone "6085551023"). The file also contains update/delete/get owner tests and nested pet/visit creation tests.

Other test files that mention owners but are not owner-creation unit tests: `src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`, `AuditLogCapture.java`, `Cp01Tests.java`, plus a JMeter plan and a Postman collection under `src/test/jmeter/` and `src/test/postman/`.

---

### Summary of the POST /api/owners flow
1. Request body JSON is bound to generated `OwnerFieldsDto` and `@Valid`-checked in `BuildOwner`; validation failure -> `MethodArgumentNotValidException` -> `ValidationExceptionHandler` -> 400 ProblemDetail.
2. `BuildOwner` maps `OwnerFieldsDto` -> `Owner` via `OwnerMapper.toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (id & pets ignored), emits `Out<Owner>`.
